	<property id="FlashClockText">
		<target>generic</target>
<name>Only CPU1 on-chip Flash Plugin can configure clock for CPU1 Flash operations.
      Plugin automatically configures PLL when CPU1 Flash operations are invoked.
      When this button is used, Flash Plugin will configure the Sysclock of 200MHz for CPU1 using 10MHZ INTOSC as the clock source. 
	  Plugin will leave PLL config like this and user application should configure the PLL as required by application. 
      Before doing any flash operations using the flash plugin, 
      (a) Please select which bank mode will be used for CPU operation - Bank Mode 0, Bank Mode 1.
      (b) Please select the flash banks that the user would like the flash plugin to erase in the flash plugin GUI.
      Note: In this version of the flash plugin, CPU1 flash applications are supported only.
</name>
		<valueType>Text</valueType>
	</property>

