	<property id="FlashProgramProtectionText">
		<target>TMS320C29XX</target>
		<name>CMDWEPROTA - Controls program/erase protection for first 32 sectors. Each bit allows users to enable/disable protection for each sector. 
Eg: Bit 0 allows protection configuration for Sector 0. A value of 0 disables protection and a value of 1 enables protection from program/erase.

CMDWEPROTB - Controls program/erase protection for sectors 32 to 255. Each bit allows users to enable/disable protection for a group of eight sectors. Note - The first 4 bit fields are reserved (bits 0 - 3) and protections overlap with CMDWEPROTA sections 22-31 (bit 4).
Eg: Bit 0 allows protection configuration for Sectors 32-255. A value of 0 disables protection and a value of 1 enables protection from program/erase.</name>
		<valueType>Text</valueType>
	</property>
	
